 "response": "**Lastal's budget is $1,025K**, assuming I copied every withdrawal link correctly. This was a long hand pass and I did not check it twice. I found two links I had missed at first and fixed them, so another slip is possible.\n\n1. **Which records count.** Only Finance Office budget updates change the budget. Messages from Sales, PMO, Facilities and the rest are ignored, and so are Finance notes that don't change the budget (audits, receipts, purchase orders, cost-center codes). The starting point is #0001, which sets the budget to $2,610K. No later record sets it again.\n\n2. **Withdrawals.** I followed each withdrawal chain back from its last link. A withdrawal counts only if no valid withdrawal targets it. Two examples:\n   - **#0062 \u2192 #0015 \u2192 #0008 \u2192 #0005:** #0062 is not withdrawn, so #0015 is cancelled. That makes #0008 valid, so the +$561K in #0005 is withdrawn.\n   - **#1505 \u2192 #1330 \u2192 #1090 \u2192 #0934 \u2192 #0462:** #1505 cancels #1330, which makes #1090 valid. #1090 cancels #0934, so the \u2212$133K in #0462 still applies.\n\n   The two links I first missed were #1314 (withdraws the +$196K in #0447) and #1428 (withdraws the +$567K in #0867).\n\n3. **Calculation.** I applied all remaining increases and decreases once each, in order, starting from $2,610K. The running total ends at $1,025K after #1598 (+$25K).\n\nANSWER: $1025K",
